# FleetFlow Core

## Session start

1. Read `memory-bank/INDEX.md`, then `activeContext.md` and `progress.md`.
2. Prefer MVP path: auth → deliveries → map → foreground GPS → WebSocket → admin live map.
3. Do not implement background location / offline queue / CI until MVP works unless asked.

## Monorepo

- Turborepo on top of npm workspaces. Root `turbo.json` owns the task graph.
- Code lives in `apps/mobile`, `apps/admin`, `apps/api`, `packages/shared-types`, `packages/config`.
- Shared enums/DTOs/WS events go in `packages/shared-types` first.
- Run tasks from the root through turbo (`npm run typecheck`, `npm run mobile`), not `cd apps/mobile`.
- Update `memory-bank/activeContext.md` + `progress.md` after meaningful milestones.

## Quality bar

- TypeScript strict; no `any` without justification.
- Thin route/screen files; logic in features/services/hooks.
- No secrets in source; use env + SecureStore for tokens.
- Keep admin thin; prioritize mobile architecture quality.

## Git workflow

- Commit each task/feature separately with a clear message.
- Never bundle unrelated changes into one commit.
- Do not push unless explicitly asked.
